<title>UK: Copper slow in LME evening, aluminium above $1,600.</title>
<headline>Copper slow in LME evening, aluminium above $1,600.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Copper prices hardly budged during Friday evening inter-office LME trading, with the market expected to re-establish upward momentum next week, traders said.</p>
<p>Prices held just above the $2,250 inter-mediate support level throughout the evening to stand at $2,255/2,260 at 1900 gmt.</p>
<p>Meanwhile, aluminiumn edged back above the $1,600 level and was quoted at $1,600/1,603.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 8080</p>
